    {
      "id": "cell_0",
      "order": 0,
      "label": "Introduction",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "# Game of Life — Gosper Glider Gun 🔫\n\n**Conway's Game of Life** is a zero-player cellular automaton devised by mathematician John Conway in 1970. The entire universe evolves from an initial seed using just three rules applied simultaneously to every cell.\n\n## Rules (B3/S23)\n\n- **Birth**: A dead cell with exactly **3** live neighbours becomes alive.\n- **Survival**: A live cell with **2 or 3** live neighbours stays alive.\n- **Death**: All other live cells die (loneliness or overcrowding).\n\n## The Gosper Glider Gun\n\nBefore 1970, theorists wondered whether any finite pattern could produce an **unbounded** number of live cells. Bill Gosper settled the question on November 23, 1970, when he discovered the **Gosper Glider Gun** — the first known finite pattern with unbounded growth.\n\nThe gun is a 36-cell oscillator with **period 30**: every 30 generations it fires a **glider** (a 5-cell \"spaceship\" that translates diagonally). The continuous stream of gliders means the total live-cell count grows without bound.\n\n### Why It Matters\n\n- It proved that Life is Turing-complete (guns can build logic gates).\n- It earned Gosper a $50 prize from Conway for solving the growth conjecture.\n- Gliders became the \"signals\" that carry information in Life computers.\n\n## This Notebook\n\n- **Cell 1** — Live 160 × 120 simulation at 15 FPS. Watch gliders stream rightward.\n- **Cell 2** — Real-time dashboard: generation counter, live-cell count, and period annotation.\n",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_1",
      "order": 1,
      "label": "Glider Gun Simulation",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "// Gosper Glider Gun — live Simulation trait implementation.\n//\n// B3/S23 rules on a 160×120 toroidal grid at 15 FPS.\n// The gun fires a glider every 30 generations indefinitely.\n\nconst W: usize = 160;\nconst H: usize = 120;\nconst CELL_SIZE: u32 = 5;\n\nstruct GliderGun {\n    grid: Vec<bool>,\n    generation: u64,\n}\n\n// ── Gosper Glider Gun cell coordinates (col, row) relative to pattern origin ──\n\nconst GUN_CELLS: &[(usize, usize)] = &[\n    // Left still-life block\n    (0, 4), (0, 5), (1, 4), (1, 5),\n    // Left oscillator section\n    (10, 4), (10, 5), (10, 6),\n    (11, 3), (11, 7),\n    (12, 2), (12, 8),\n    (13, 2), (13, 8),\n    (14, 5),\n    (15, 3), (15, 7),\n    (16, 4), (16, 5), (16, 6),\n    (17, 5),\n    // Right oscillator section\n    (20, 2), (20, 3), (20, 4),\n    (21, 2), (21, 3), (21, 4),\n    (22, 1), (22, 5),\n    (24, 0), (24, 1), (24, 5), (24, 6),\n    // Right still-life block\n    (34, 2), (34, 3), (35, 2), (35, 3),\n];\n\n// ── B3/S23 step ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nfn step(grid: &[bool]) -> (Vec<bool>, u64) {\n    let mut next = vec![false; W * H];\n    let mut live = 0u64;\n    for y in 0..H {\n        for x in 0..W {\n            let mut n = 0u8;\n            for dy in [H - 1, 0, 1] {\n                for dx in [W - 1, 0, 1] {\n                    if dy == 0 && dx == 0 { continue; }\n                    let ny = (y + dy) % H;\n                    let nx = (x + dx) % W;\n                    if grid[ny * W + nx] { n += 1; }\n                }\n            }\n            let alive = n == 3 || (n == 2 && grid[y * W + x]);\n            next[y * W + x] = alive;\n            if alive { live += 1; }\n        }\n    }\n    (next, live)\n}\n\n// ── Simulation trait ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nimpl Simulation for GliderGun {\n    fn init() -> Self {\n        let mut grid = vec![false; W * H];\n        // Place the gun in the upper-left quadrant with a small margin.\n        let (ox, oy) = (2usize, 5usize);\n        for &(gx, gy) in GUN_CELLS {\n            let x = ox + gx;\n            let y = oy + gy;\n            if x < W && y < H {\n                grid[y * W + x] = true;\n            }\n        }\n        Self { grid, generation: 0 }\n    }\n\n    fn tick(&mut self) -> Canvas {\n        let (next, live) = step(&self.grid);\n        self.grid = next;\n        self.generation += 1;\n\n        sim::emit(\"generation\", &self.generation);\n        sim::emit(\"live_cells\", &live);\n\n        // Render: bright phosphor-green alive cells on a dark CRT background.\n        Canvas::from_fn(W as u32 * CELL_SIZE, H as u32 * CELL_SIZE, |x, y| {\n            let gx = (x / CELL_SIZE) as usize;\n            let gy = (y / CELL_SIZE) as usize;\n            if self.grid[gy * W + gx] {\n                (0, 255, 100) // phosphor green\n            } else {\n                (10, 10, 20) // dark CRT background\n            }\n        })\n    }\n\n    fn fps() -> u32 { 15 }\n}\n",
      "cargo_toml": null,
      "collapsed": true
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_2",
      "order": 2,
      "label": "Statistics Dashboard",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "// Gosper Glider Gun — real-time statistics dashboard (LiveView).\n//\n// Reads generation and live-cell counts from the simulation bus and renders\n// a retro terminal-style HTML panel at 5 FPS.\n\nstruct Stats {\n    tick: u32,\n}\n\nimpl LiveView for Stats {\n    fn init() -> Self {\n        Self { tick: 0 }\n    }\n\n    fn tick(&mut self) -> LiveContent {\n        self.tick += 1;\n\n        let gen   = sim::read::<u64>(\"generation\").unwrap_or(0);\n        let cells = sim::read::<u64>(\"live_cells\").unwrap_or(0);\n\n        // Every 30 generations the gun fires one glider.\n        let gliders_fired = gen / 30;\n        // Highlight cell count: it grows as more gliders are in flight.\n        let cell_color = if cells > 100 { \"#66ff88\" } else { \"#00cc55\" };\n\n        let period_bar_pct = (gen % 30) * 100 / 29;\n\n        let html = format!(\n            r#\"<div style=\"background:#0a0a14;color:#b8ffc8;padding:20px 24px;border-radius:8px;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;max-width:480px;border:1px solid #1a3a2a;line-height:1.7;\">\n  <div style=\"color:#33ff77;font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:2px;margin-bottom:14px;border-bottom:1px solid #1a3a2a;padding-bottom:8px;\">\n    ◼ GOSPER GLIDER GUN — TELEMETRY\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:160px 1fr;row-gap:8px;column-gap:12px;font-size:13px;\">\n    <span style=\"color:#668866;\">Generation</span>\n    <span style=\"color:#ffffff;font-size:16px;font-weight:bold;\">{gen}</span>\n    <span style=\"color:#668866;\">Live Cells</span>\n    <span style=\"color:{cell_color};font-size:16px;font-weight:bold;\">{cells}</span>\n    <span style=\"color:#668866;\">Gliders Fired</span>\n    <span style=\"color:#88ddff;\">{gliders_fired}</span>\n    <span style=\"color:#668866;\">Gun Period</span>\n    <span style=\"color:#ffcc44;\">30 generations</span>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"margin-top:16px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size:11px;color:#558855;margin-bottom:4px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;\">Period Progress ({phase}/29)</div>\n    <div style=\"background:#0f1f0f;border-radius:4px;height:8px;overflow:hidden;\">\n      <div style=\"background:linear-gradient(90deg,#00aa44,#00ff88);height:100%;width:{period_bar_pct}%;transition:width 0.1s;\"></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"margin-top:14px;font-size:11px;color:#446644;border-top:1px solid #1a3a2a;padding-top:8px;\">\n    ▸ Discovered by Bill Gosper, 1970 &nbsp;|&nbsp; B3/S23 rules &nbsp;|&nbsp; First finite infinite-growth pattern\n  </div>\n</div>\"#,\n            gen = gen,\n            cells = cells,\n            cell_color = cell_color,\n            gliders_fired = gliders_fired,\n            period_bar_pct = period_bar_pct,\n            phase = gen % 30,\n        );\n\n        LiveContent::Html(html)\n    }\n\n    fn fps() -> u32 { 5 }\n}\n",
      "cargo_toml": null,
      "collapsed": true
    }
  ]
}